{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>From the wilderness of Zin to Rehob, at Lebo-hamath.</b> They walked its borders in length and in breadth in a gamma shape. They walked the southern border from the eastern corner to the western corner, as Moses commanded: ״go up this way by the Negev״ — along the southeastern border to the sea — for the sea is the western border. From there they turned back and walked the entire western border along the edge of the sea until Lebo-hamath, which is near Mount Hor at the northwestern corner, as is spelled out in the borders of the land in the parashah of These are the Journeys."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:42.079688069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}